}

\p{The join is by declaration name. The machine's units are the definitions, theorems, opaque constants and axioms; inductive types, constructors and recursors are checked by the driver between two units. All units of the three corpora are joined (gruszka 98.5 \% / 99.2 \% / 98.7 \%, nano-lean 98.0 \% / 99.3 \% / 99.5 \% of their per-declaration instructions are in the joined units). "Origin" of a unit: Init, Std, Mathlib-and-dependencies = the name is a unit of the arena's \code{\verb~|init~}, \code{\verb~|std~}, \code{\verb~|mathlib~} export (P8's unit lists) or a private name of those libraries; else the project's own.}

\p{A unit the machine declines is in the join with what the machine spent before declining (both attempts); the reference engine's work on it is outside \code{\verb~|Session.check~} and appears only as thread CPU between two checks. Over the units the machine itself decides the ratios to gruszka are 8.04 (navier-stokes-euler), 4.29 (cslib), 3.25 (con-leche) instead of 7.98, 4.12, 3.24.}

\p{The whole process: 972 G instructions on navier-stokes-euler (48,623 samples x 20,000,003; the integrator's table says 973.2 G), of which 886.4 G inside the checks; 757 G / 587.0 G on cslib; 174 G / 146.9 G on con-leche.}

\p{E1 published a machine jar with fixes of wrong accepts at 21:26Z (5945b6568177); it is NOT what was measured.}
}

