\p{With the options the machine does gruszka's number of operations on navier-stokes-euler (1.11 times its ticks, 0.78 times its values) at 3.3 times its instructions per tick; on con-leche it does so without them. The largest units of navier-stokes-euler show it one by one: \code{\verb~|NavierStokes.FiveProfileMoments.quadraticBilin._proof_6~} (0.94 \% of the machine's corpus, 2.0 \% of gruszka's): machine 3,632,559 ticks, 415,947 INFER + 92,549 CHECK, 206,156 CONV + 346,046 pair hits, 184,549 DELTA; with the options 2,031,456 ticks and 9,294 DELTA; gruszka 3,068,095 ticks, 377,684 infer misses, 413,352 def_eq calls (296,817 cache hits), 8,588 unfoldings: the same work, 7.38 G against 2.28 G instructions (3.2 times; nano-lean 1.97 G).}

