\subtree{
\title{6. What could not be established}

\ul{
\li{\strong{gruszka's CPU time per unit on quiet cores.} Its instructions and counters per declaration are exact; the seconds quoted for it (0.13 s, 1.04 s, 0.72 s, the 6 - 7 G instructions per second) are its own clock from the profile run in a container on CPUs 18 and 19 while the host was loaded, with a marker line per declaration. The CPU ratios of point 8 of section 0 are therefore directions; the integrator's table is the quiet comparison of the whole processes.}
\li{\strong{The machine with E1's fixes} (jar 5945b6568177 of 21:26Z and what follows): everything here is jar 15cb3777e598. The fixes change inference; I did not measure them.}
\li{\strong{The warm wall clock with 8 workers}: everything is one worker, cold process, batch load.}
\li{\strong{How much of class 4.2 is B12 (closure congruence) and how much B1 (same-head probe)}: the two are one option. The trace shows the closure case; the counters of the options run say B1 answered T 4.1 M times and B12 0.9 M times, which is not a cost split.}
\li{\strong{Whether an official-exact form of 4.1 / 4.2 exists}: C1's report says no for 4.1; 4.2 ("entries convertible, not identical") is the same question for closures and I did not examine it.}
\li{\strong{What the reference fallback's 2.4 ms per declined unit consists of} (it is not proportional to the reference steps): engine start, import of the unit, the steps themselves were not separated.}
\li{\strong{Instructions of the inductive blocks on the machine's side} (only thread CPU of the gaps), and which blocks.}
\li{\strong{The session cap in CPU time on navier-stokes-euler and cslib}; con-leche only (section 4.5).}
\li{The origin classification uses the arena's \code{\verb~|mathlib~} export as "Mathlib and its dependencies"; 683 units of navier-stokes-euler are private names of Mathlib modules that are not in that export (another Mathlib version) and were assigned by their module name.}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{7. Reproduction}

\pre{\verb~|
P=work/prof/P9
# the tap jar and the native image (published jars of 21:02Z + P8's tap)
bench/slot.sh -c ni -n 2 -- $P/build-ni.sh $P/dist-tap
# leaders per declaration (Docker): base/<corpus>/gruszka.w1.di, gruszka-cnt.raw, nano-lean.j1.trace
bench/slot.sh -- bench/arena-docker.sh --cpuset-cpus 18,19 --memory 16g --no-network \
    $P/base-leaders.sh navier-stokes-euler con-leche cslib
# machine, instructions per unit (Docker): data/units-t-*.tsv, data/instr-t-*.txt
bench/slot.sh -- bench/arena-docker.sh --cpuset-cpus 18,19 --memory 16g --no-network \
    $P/batch-instr.sh navier-stokes-euler con-leche cslib          # t-def, t-dfp, t-dfp-cong
bench/slot.sh -- bench/arena-docker.sh --cpuset-cpus 18,19 --memory 16g --no-network \
    $P/batch-split.sh navier-stokes-euler cslib con-leche          # t-df-skip, t-dfp-congonly
# machine, events per op (host): data/units-n-*.tsv, data/stats-n-*.json
$P/run-tap.sh native n-def navier-stokes-euler default
# tables
python3 -I $P/scripts/report.py navier-stokes-euler   > $P/out/report-navier-stokes-euler.md
python3 -I $P/scripts/optsplit.py navier-stokes-euler > $P/out/optsplit-navier-stokes-euler.md
python3 -I $P/scripts/doctables.py                    > $P/out/doctables.md
python3 -I $P/scripts/quietcpu.py navier-stokes-euler > $P/out/quiet-navier-stokes-euler.md
# traces of named units (private machine copy with hooks, JVM): out/trace-TAG.txt
$P/run-trace.sh nse-def navier-stokes-euler default Name1,Name2 [-Dp9.log=4000 -Dp9.clip=420]
python3 -I $P/scripts/tracesum.py $P/out/trace-nse-def.txt
# flat instruction profile (Docker) and the quiet windows
bench/slot.sh -- bench/arena-docker.sh --cpuset-cpus 18,19 --memory 16g --no-network $P/batch-perf.sh
bench/quiet.py -- $P/quiet-run.sh ; bench/quiet.py -- $P/quiet-run2.sh
~}

\p{Files: \code{\verb~|data/units-*.tsv~} (one line per check), \code{\verb~|data/instr-*.txt~}, \code{\verb~|data/stats-*.json~}, \code{\verb~|base/<corpus>/*~} (leaders), \code{\verb~|out/report-*.md~} (all tables per corpus, with the 40 worst units), \code{\verb~|out/optsplit-*.md~}, \code{\verb~|out/quiet-*.md~}, \code{\verb~|out/trace-*.txt~}, \code{\verb~|out/perf-*.ips~}, \code{\verb~|logs/runs.log~} (every run with its switches), \code{\verb~|logs/quiet.times~}.}
}
